upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/skills/main/skills/wrangler/SKILL.md
verified: 2026-09-29
scope: directory
reason: One deliberate line. SKILL.md body is byte-identical to upstream (last path commit 320fbbc1);
  only the frontmatter description appends "Not for Worker code review (workers-best-practices)
  or product choice (cloudflare)." (236 characters total). Codex keeps only ~240 characters of
  each description, and upstream's has no boundary, so the sibling boundary is front-loaded here,
  matching the cloudflare and durable-objects forks.
retired: the 2026-08-16 fork reasons are gone. The manual split was dropped with upstream's
  rewrite, and the stale "wrangler dev --remote ... (legacy)" wording no longer exists upstream
  (the new SKILL.md defers flags to project-local --help and the command docs). The Previews
  claim "Wrangler 4.135.0 or later" was checked against
  https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/previews/get-started/ on 2026-09-29 and matches.
would_lose_if_wired: a byte-for-byte refresh would drop the sibling boundary from the description.
refresh_guard: _refresh-vendored.sh skips this directory when .local-fork is present.
to_vendor: remove this ledger (and become byte-identical) if upstream adds an equivalent boundary
  or the Codex description cut stops mattering.
